# Block33 assumptions and imports

| ID | role | exact content | status |
|---|---|---|---|
| A0 | foundation | the four current framework axioms at preregistered `origin/main` | approved premise |
| A1 | pair law | Block28/32 symbolic `q_lambda` on sixteen complete returned-pair Record outcomes, `0 <= lambda < 1` | conditional imported construction |
| A2 | two-use target | Block32's conditional second row is the same `q_lambda`, so the declared two-use outcome law is `q_lambda tensor q_lambda` | conditional imported construction |
| C1 | screening class | a finite classical cause `Z`, weights `pi_z`, and product responses `r_z(g,h)=a_z(g)b_z(h)` | explicit tested architecture, not framework content |
| C2 | frozen stationary history | the same unchanged `Z` is used twice with the identical conditional kernel, `P(X_1=x,X_2=y|Z=z)=r_z(x)r_z(y)`; the conditional response noise is fresh on each use | explicit conditionally iid tested grammar, not reuse of one complete environment |
| C3 | supplied-iid control | a new iid five-state `Z_t` with law `(1-lambda,lambda/4,...,lambda/4)` and a disjoint fresh output/archive bank are supplied at each event to one fixed response/isometry | explicit finite positive control, not a derived reset or renewal theorem |
| C4 | coherent control | a uniform first label and one proper-cubic-covariant `U_lambda` produce the second label through squared amplitudes | explicit alternate realization |
| C5 | depth-three control | a positive three-event law may depend on prior outcomes while all of its two-event marginals are product | explicit process counterfamily |

The fixed isometry uses an abstract orthogonal five-sector program/cause
register, retains that register and the local seed in the output/archive, and
starts from explicit Blank output/archive banks.  Normalization is not
obtained by silently discarding a resource.  It is an abstract finite
dilation, not a local `M_2(C)` carrier or reset law.

`Factorization-neutral` in this packet means only that the frozen-cause proof
covers every finite nonnegative product-response factorization in C1.  It
does not mean neutral across hidden non-screening, quantum/entangled,
direct-joint, evolving-memory, or extensive-environment realizations.

The general C1 cause is not assumed visible, copyable, orthogonal, minimal, or
a framework Record.  The specific C3 controlled-isometry control does use an
abstract orthogonal five-sector register.  `Frozen stationary` means its value
is unchanged and the same response `r_z` is used across the two conditionally
independent draws, while the response randomness itself is fresh.  A frozen
cause with use-dependent response kernels lies outside C2.  `Supplied iid`
means disjoint cause/output/archive inputs are present initially; it does not
mean a local reset channel has been constructed.  The conditional product
history A2 is not promoted to an autonomous global process.

`Physical renewal` would require the framework dynamics itself to restore or
replenish a consumed cause/output/archive resource, with its source and debit
modeled.  Block33 does not test or claim that stronger condition.
